Implementation Notes
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

   This file is used by the SPICE system as follows: programs that make
   use of this kernel must ``load'' the kernel, normally during program
   initialization. The SPICE routine FURNSH loads a kernel file into
   the pool as shown below.

      CALL FURNSH ( 'frame_kernel_name; )    -- FORTRAN
      furnsh_c ( "frame_kernel_name" );      -- C
      cspice_furnsh, frame_kernel_name       -- IDL
      cspice_furnsh( 'frame_kernel_name' )   -- MATLAB

   Once the file has been loaded, the SPICE routine GETFOV (getfov_c in
   C, cspice_getfov in IDL and MATLAB) can be used to retrieve FOV
   parameters for a given instrument or structure.

   This file was created and may be updated with a text editor or word
   processor.


Conventions for Specifying Data
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

   Data items are specified using ``keyword=value'' assignments [1].
   All keywords referencing values in this I-kernel start with the
   characters `INS' followed by the NAIF LICIA instrument ID code,
   constructed using the spacecraft ID number (-210) followed by the
   NAIF three digit ID number for LICIA_LEIA (100) . These
   IDs are defined in [4] as follows:

               Instrument name          ID
               --------------------   -------
               LICIA_LEIA              -210100
               LICIA_LUKE              -210200

   The remainder of the keyword is an underscore character followed by the
   unique name of the data item. For example, the focal length of the
   LICIA_LEIA is specified by

               INS-210100_FOCAL_LENGTH

   The upper bound on the length of all keywords is 32 characters.

   If a keyword is included in more than one file, or if the same
   keyword appears more than once within a single file, the last
   assignment supersedes any earlier assignments.


Overview
---------------------------------------------------------------------------


Summary of LICIA LEIA Characteristics
-----------------------------------------------------------

         Wavelength range (nm):
            
            LEIA -- 400 - 900

         Image scale (microradians per pixel):
            
            LEIA -- 25

         Field of view (degrees):
            
            Narrow angle camera -- 2.93 x 2.93

         Optical design:
            
            Narrow angle camera -- Catadioptric 2 Mirrors 3 lenses

         F-ratio:
            
            Narrow angle camera -- 3.0

         Focal length (mm):
            
            Narrow angle camera -- 222.5

         Mass (including harness, kg):
            0.89

         Power consumption (maximum, W):
            Static Mode 1.5 
                        Pixel reset 2.5 


Summary of LICIA LUKE Characteristics
-----------------------------------------------------------      

         Wavelength range (nm):
            
            LUKE -- 450 - 700

         Image scale (microradians per pixel):
            
            LUKE -- 78

         Field of view (degrees):
            
            WIDE angle camera -- 4.8 x 9.15

         Optical design:
            
            WIDE angle camera -- Dioptric 4 lenses

         F-ratio:
            
            wide angle camera -- 2.2

         Focal length (mm):
            
            wide angle camera -- 70.5

         Mass (including harness, kg):
            0.39

         Power consumption (maximum, W):
            Static Mode 1.65 
                        Imaging mode 2.85 

         Color Filters 
                        Bayer Filter


